# Symbulator circuit book

title: Circuits for Lesson 7 of the Tutorial

[AS7's Example 9.9]

e,1,0,10
r1,1,2,5
c,2,0,.1

analysis: ac
note: In this problem, we run an AC (phasor) analysis for the first time: find v(t) and i(t). The first AC problem. The source is the phasor of 10 cos(4t), and the capacitor is in farads, which is why the frequency is needed. Read ir1 and vc with the aa mini-tool, then convert back to sinusoids by hand.
omega: 4
rounding: 4
si: no
units: yes
rms: no
polar: yes


[AS7's Practice Problem 9.9]

e,1,0,(20∠30°)
r1,1,2,4
l,2,0,.2

analysis: ac
note: Find v(t) and i(t) — read ir1 and vl. The source is written in polar form, which version 9 reads as typed.
omega: 10
rounding: 4
si: no
units: yes
rms: no
polar: yes


[AS7's Example 9.10]

ca,1,2,2'm
r1,2,3,3
cb,3,0,10'm
l1,2,4,.2
r2,4,0,8

analysis: ac
note: Find the input impedance of the circuit at ω = 50 rad/s. A passive network, so the Resistance / impedance equivalent between nodes 1 and 0 does it: zeq = 3.22 - 11.07j ohm.
omega: 50
tool: er
n1: 1
n2: 0
rounding: 4
si: no
units: yes
rms: no
polar: no


